{"r":"Ery","lane":{"p":2029,"e":[{"h":"عَرِىَ","t":["(S, MA, Mgh, Msb, K) ",[2,"مِنْ ثِيَابِهِ"],", (S, MA, Mgh, Msb,) aor. ",[2,"يَعْرَى"],", (S, Msb,) inf. n. ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"]," (Mgh, Msb, K, and so in some copies of the S, accord. to other copies of which it is ",[2,"عُرِىٌّ"],", and also with kesr to the ",[2,"ع"],", as stated in the TA, [",[2,"العُرٰى"]," commencing the art. in the CK is a mistake for ",[2,"العُرْىُ"],",]) and ",[2,"عُرْيَةٌ"],", (Msb, K,) ",[1,"He"]," (a man, Msb, TA) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, naked, nude, bare,"]," or ",[1,"without clothing;"]," (K, TA;) or ",[1,"bare of his clothes:"]," (MA:) and ↓ ",[2,"تعرّى"]," signifies the same: (MA, K:) [or rather] the latter is quasipass. of ",[2,"عرّاهُ"]," [and therefore is more correctly rendered ",[1,"he was made naked,"]," &c.; or ",[1,"made bare of his clothes,"]," or ",[1,"denuded thereof,"]," or ",[1,"divested;"]," or ",[1,"he made himself naked,"]," &c.; or ",[1,"denuded himself of his clothes"],"]. (S.) [And sometimes it means ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, bare of clothing,"]," or ",[1,"of his clothes, except one,"]," or ",[1,"more, of his inner garments:"]," and in like manner, ↓ ",[2,"تعرّى"],", ",[1,"he was made,"]," or ",[1,"he made himself, bare of clothing,"]," or ",[1,"of his clothes, except one,"]," or ",[1,"more, of his inner garments."],"] ― -b2- And [hence] one says also, ",[2,"عَرِىَ البَدَنُ مِنَ اللَّحْمِ"]," [",[1,"The body was,"]," or ",[1,"became, bare of flesh,"]," or ",[1,"lean"],"]. (TA.) ― -b3- And ",[2,"عَرِىَ مِنَ العَيْبِ"],", aor. as above, (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, was,"]," or ",[1,"became, free from fault, defect,"]," or ",[1,"blemish:"]," part. n. ↓ ",[2,"عَرٍ"]," [if not a mistranscription for ",[2,"عَارٍ"],"]. (Msb.) And ",[2,"عَرِىَ مِنَ"],[2,"الأَمْرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, free from the affair:"]," and ",[2,"مَا يَعْرَى مِنْ هٰذَا الأَمْرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He is not,"]," or ",[1,"does not become, free from this affair:"]," and hence, ",[2,"لَا"],[2,"يَعْرَى مِنَ المَوْتِ أَحَدٌ"]," (assumed tropical:) [",[1,"No one will be exempt from death"],"]. (TA.) -A2- ",[2,"عَرَيْتُهُ"],[1,"I came to him;"]," syn. ",[2,"غَشِيتُهُ"],"; like ",[2,"عَرَوْتُهُ"]," [q. v.]. (K.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"عَرَّىَ","t":["see 4. ― -b2- [Hence,] one says also, ",[2,"عرّاهُ مِنَ"],[2,"الأَمْرِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He freed him from the affair."]," (TA.) ― -b3- And ",[2,"عَرَّيْتُهُ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"I left it;"]," or ",[1,"let it alone;"]," i. e., anything. (TA.)"],"f":"2"},{"h":"نَحْنُ نُعَارِى","t":[[1,"We ride the horses not saddled."]," (K, TA.) [See also 12.]"],"f":"3"},{"h":"اعراهُ","t":["(S, MA, Msb, K) ",[2,"مِنْ ثِيَابِهِ"],", (Msb,) or ",[2,"مِنَ الثِّيَابِ"],", (MA,) or ",[2,"الثَّوْبَ"]," and ",[2,"مِنَ الثَّوْبِ"],"; (K;) and ↓ ",[2,"عرّاهُ"],", (S, MA, Msb, K,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَعْرِيَةٌ"],"; (S, K;) ",[1,"He denuded him, made him bare,"]," or ",[1,"divested him,"]," (S, * MA, Msb, * K,) ",[1,"of his clothes,"]," (Msb,) or ",[1,"of the clothes,"]," (MA,) or ",[1,"of the garment."]," (K.) ― -b2- And ",[2,"اعراهُ"]," signifies also ",[1,"He plucked out the hair of his"]," (a horse's) ",[1,"tail;"]," like ",[2,"أَعَارَهُ"],": mentioned by IKtt and others. (TA in art. ",[2,"عير"],".) ― -b3- See also three other significations (two of which seem to belong to this art.) in art. ",[2,"عرو"],". -A2- ",[2,"اعرى"]," as intrans. ",[1,"He"]," (a man, TA) ",[1,"journeyed in"]," [",[1,"a bare and wide tract,"]," or] ",[1,"what is termed"],[2,"عَرَآء"]," [q. v.]: and ",[1,"he remained, stayed, dwelt,"]," or ",[1,"abode, therein."]," (K, TA.) And ",[1,"He remained, stayed, dwelt,"]," or ",[1,"abode, in the lateral,"]," or ",[1,"adjacent, part"]," or ",[1,"tract"]," (",[2,"بِالنَّاحِيَةِ"],"). (TA.) And ",[2,"أَعْرَيْتُ"]," signifies also ",[2,"اِجْتَنَبْتُ"]," [app. as meaning ",[1,"I was,"]," or ",[1,"became, distant, remote, far off,"]," or ",[1,"aloof;"]," or ",[1,"I went,"]," or ",[1,"removed,"]," or ",[1,"retired,"]," or ",[1,"withdrew myself, to a distance,"]," or ",[1,"far away;"]," though I do not know ",[2,"اجتنبت"]," used otherwise than as trans.]; as also ↓ ",[2,"اِسْتَعْرَيْتُ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"اِعْتَرَيْتُ"],": mentioned by Sgh. (TA.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"تَعَرَّىَ","t":["see the first paragraph, in two places."],"f":"5"},{"h":"إِعْتَرَىَ","t":["see 4, last sentence."],"f":"8"},{"h":"إِسْتَعْرَىَ","t":["see 4, last sentence: -A2- and see 10 in art. ",[2,"عرو"],"."],"f":"10"},{"h":"اعرورى الفَرَسَ","t":["(S, K,) or ",[2,"الدَّابَّةَ"],", (Mgh, Msb,) ",[1,"He rode the horse,"]," or ",[1,"the beast, without a saddle,"]," (S, Mgh, Msb, K, * and Ham p. 42,) ",[1,"and having nothing beneath him;"]," (Ham:) the verb being of the measure ",[2,"اِفْعَوْعَلَ"],", (S, TA,) a measure of which there is no other trans. v. except ",[2,"اِحْلَوْلَى"],". (TA.) ― -b2- Hence the usage of the verb in the saying of Taäbbata-Sharrà ",[2,"يَظَلُّ بِمَوْمَاةٍ وَيُمْسِى بِغَيْرِهَا"],[2,"جَحِيشًا وَيَعْرَوْرِى ظُهُورَ المَهَالِكِ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He passes the day in a waterless desert, and enters upon the evening in another than it, alone, and he ventures upon"]," [",[1,"the surfaces of"],"] ",[1,"the places of perdition without anything to protect him from them."]," (Ham ubi suprà.) [See also an ex. of the act. part. n. in a verse cited in the second paragraph of art. ",[2,"دوم"],".] ― -b3- And ",[2,"اعرورى السَّرَابُ الآكَامَ"]," means ",[2,"رَكِبَهَا"]," [i. e. (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The mirage surmounted the hills,"]," or ",[1,"mounds"],"]. (TA.) ― -b4- And ",[2,"اعرورى أَمْرًا"],[2,"قَبِيحًا"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He ventured upon,"]," or ",[1,"did, an evil,"]," or ",[1,"a foul, thing;"]," (S, K; *) syn. ",[2,"رَكِبَهُ"],", (S,) or ",[2,"أَتَاهُ"],", (K,) or both. (TA.) ― -b5- ",[2,"اعرورى"]," signifies also (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"He journeyed by himself, alone, in the earth,"]," or ",[1,"land."]," (K.)"],"f":"12"},{"h":"عَرًى","t":[[1,"A hard and elevated,"]," or ",[1,"an elevated and plain, part,"]," or ",[1,"tract,"]," of the earth, ",[1,"that is apparent,"]," or ",[1,"open:"]," pl. ",[2,"أَعْرَآءٌ"],". (TA.) [",[2,"عَرَآءٌ"],", also, (q. v.,) has a similar meaning, and the same pl.] ― -b2- And ",[1,"i. q."],[2,"حَائِطٌ"]," [",[1,"A wall;"]," or ",[1,"a wall of enclosure;"]," or ",[1,"one that surrounds a garden:"]," or ",[1,"a garden,"]," in general; or ",[1,"a garden of palm-trees, surrounded by a wall"],"]. (TA.) ― -b3- See also ",[2,"عَرًا"]," in art. ",[2,"عرو"],": and in the same paragraph see its syn. ",[2,"عَرَاةٌ"],"."]},{"h":"عَرٍ","t":[": see 1, last quarter."]},{"h":"عُرْىٌ","t":["A horse ",[1,"not having a saddle upon him;"]," (S, Msb, K;) and so ↓ ",[2,"مُعْرَوْرٍ"]," and ↓ ",[2,"مُعْرَوْرًى"],": (TA:) or ",[1,"not having upon him a saddle nor a saddle-cloth,"]," or ",[1,"housing;"]," as also ↓ ",[2,"مُعْرَوْرًى"],"; but ↓ ",[2,"مُعْرَوْرٍ"]," signifies ",[1,"riding without a saddle and without a saddle-cloth,"]," or ",[1,"housing:"]," (Mgh:) or ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"]," [as also ↓ ",[2,"مُعْرَوْرًى"],"] signifies ",[1,"not having upon him a saddle nor any furniture:"]," (TA:) ↓ ",[2,"عُرْيَانٌ"]," is not applied as an epithet to a horse, nor is ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"]," to a man: (Mgh, Msb, TA:) the latter is an inf. n. used as an epithet, and then made a subst., having a pl., (Msb, TA,) which is ",[2,"أَعْرَآءٌ"],". (S, Mgh, Msb, TA.)"]},{"h":"جَارِيَةٌ حَسَنَةُ العُرْيَةِ","t":["and ↓ ",[2,"العِرْيَةِ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"المَعْرَى"],", and ↓ ",[2,"المَعْرَاةِ"],", (K, TA,) or, as in the M, ↓ ",[2,"المُعَرَّى"],", and ↓ ",[2,"المَعْرَاةِ"],", and in like manner in the A, ↓ ",[2,"المُعَرَّى"]," and ",[2,"العُرْيَة"]," being [there] said to be like ",[2,"المُجَرَّد"]," and ",[2,"الجُرْدَة"]," in measure and in meaning, (TA,) signify ",[2,"حَسَنَةُ المُجَرَّدِ"],", (K, TA,) i. e. [",[1,"A girl,"]," or ",[1,"young woman, beautiful in respect of what is unclad"]," of her person; or] ",[1,"beautiful when she is unclad:"]," (TA: [see also ",[2,"جُرْدَةٌ"],": the CK, for ",[2,"وَالمَعْرَى وَالمَعْرَاةِ أَىِ المُجَرَّدِ"],", has ",[2,"والمُعْرٰى والمُعْراةُ"],[2,"اَىِ المُجَرَّدُ"],":]) and ↓ ",[2,"المَعَارِى"]," (of which the sing. is ",[2,"مَعْرًى"],", TA) signifies ",[1,"the hands"]," or ",[1,"arms, and the feet"]," or ",[1,"legs, and the face,"]," (S, K, TA,) as being ",[1,"the parts that are seen,"]," (K, TA,) of a woman: (S, TA:) so in the saying, ",[2,"مَا أَحْسَنَ مَعَارِىَ هٰذِهِ"],[2,"المَرْأَةِ"]," [",[1,"How beautiful are the hands"]," or ",[1,"arms, &c., of this woman!"],"]: (S, TA:) or, as some say, ",[1,"the parts where the bones appear"]," [",[1,"as distinct"],"] ",[1,"from the flesh:"]," or, some say, ",[1,"what are necessarily made to appear,"]," of a woman: and, some say, ",[1,"the"],[2,"عَوْرَة"]," [or ",[1,"pudenda"]," of a woman]: and the ",[2,"فَرْج"]," [or ",[1,"vulva"],"]. (TA.)"]},{"h":"العِرْيَة","t":[": see the next preceding paragraph."]},{"h":"عُرْيَانٌ","t":["and ↓ ",[2,"عَارٍ"],[1,"Naked, nude, bare,"]," or ",[1,"without clothing;"]," (S, * MA, Mgh, * Msb, * K, TA;) applied to a man: (Msb, TA:) fem. ",[2,"عُرْيَانَةٌ"]," (S, MA, Mgh, &c.) and ↓ ",[2,"عَارِيَةٌ"],", (MA, Mgh, Msb, &c.,) applied to a woman: (S, Msb:) the pl. of ",[2,"عُرْيَانٌ"]," is ",[2,"عُرْيَانُونَ"],"; (K;) and the pl. of ↓ ",[2,"عَارٍ"]," is ",[2,"عُرَاةٌ"],", (Msb, K,) and that of ",[2,"عَارِيَةٌ"]," is ",[2,"عَارِيَاتٌ"],". (Msb.) [Also, sometimes, ",[1,"Bare of clothing,"]," or ",[1,"of his clothes, except one,"]," or ",[1,"more, of his inner garments."],"] See also ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"],". ― -b2- ",[2,"عُرْيَانٌ"]," applied to sand, (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"An extended and gibbous tract"]," (",[2,"نَقًا"],"), or ",[1,"such as is accumulated and congested"]," (",[2,"عَقِدٌ"],", in the CK ",[2,"عَقْدٌ"],"), of sand, ",[1,"having no trees upon it."]," (ISd, K, TA.) ― -b3- Applied to a plant, or to herbage, (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Such as has become apparent."]," (TA.) ― -b4- ",[2,"عُرْيَانُ النَّجِىِّ"]," is an appellation applied to (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"A wife:"]," but in the A it is implied that it is used as denoting anyone ",[1,"who will not conceal a secret."]," (TA.) ― -b5- ",[2,"عُرْيَانٌ"]," applied to a horse signifies (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Light,"]," or ",[1,"active, and quick; tall; and long in the legs."]," (K, TA. [Expl. in the K and TA by the words ",[2,"مُقَلّص طَوِيل"]," ; to which is added in the TA ",[2,"القَوَائِم"],": the first of these words I find written, in copies of the K, only ",[2,"مُقَلَّص"],"; but it is correctly ",[2,"مُقَلِّص"],".])"]},{"h":"عَرَآءٌ","t":["[is app. a subst. signifying ",[1,"Nakedness,"]," or ",[1,"bareness,"]," or ",[1,"the like:"]," for ",[2,"عَرَآءُ العِظَامِ مِنَ اللَّحْمِ"]," occurs in the TA, in art. ",[2,"عجف"],", evidently as meaning ",[1,"Leanness of the bones."]," -A2- Also] ",[1,"A wide,"]," or ",[1,"spacious, place"]," or ",[1,"tract of land,"]," (S, M, Msb, K,) ",[1,"in which is nothing that hides,"]," or ",[1,"conceals,"]," (S, Msb,) or ",[1,"in which nothing will be hidden,"]," (M, TA,) or ",[1,"in which one will not be hidden by anything;"]," (K;) occurring in the Kur xxxvii. 145 [and lxviii. 49]: (S:) or the ",[1,"vacant surface of the earth"]," or ",[1,"land,"]," or ",[1,"of a wide space of land:"]," (TA in this art.:) or ",[1,"a tract such as is termed"],[2,"جَهْرَآءُ"]," [q. v.]: (TA in art. ",[2,"جهر"],":) pl. ",[2,"أَعْرَآءٌ"],". (K.) [In the TA in art. ",[2,"جهر"]," the pl. is said to be ",[2,"أَعْرِيَةٌ"],". See also ",[2,"عَرَى"],".]"]},{"h":"عَارٍ","t":["; and its fem., with ",[2,"ة"],": see ",[2,"عُرْيَانٌ"],", in three places. ― -b2- [Hence,] ",[2,"عَارِى الأَشَاجِعِ"],": see ",[2,"أَشْجَعُ"],". ",[2,"عَارِى الثَّنْدُؤَتَيْنِ"]," means ",[1,"Having no flesh on the"],[2,"ثَنْدُؤَتَانِ"]," [or ",[1,"two paps"],"]. (TA.) ― -b3- And [hence] one says, ",[2,"الحَقُّ عَارٍ"]," (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The truth is"]," [",[1,"naked,"]," i. e.] ",[1,"manifest."]," (TA in art. ",[2,"عجز"],".)"]},{"h":"طَرِيقٌ اعرورى","t":["[thus I find the latter word, like the verb (12), and without any syll. signs, perhaps a mistranscription, and, if so, it may be correctly ",[2,"عَرَوْرًى"],", of the measure ",[2,"فَعَوْعَلٌ"],", like ",[2,"شَجَوْجًى"]," &c.,] ",[1,"A rugged road."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"المَعْرَى","t":["; and its pl., ",[2,"المَعَارِى"],": see ",[2,"العُرْيَة"],". ― -b2- [The pl.] ",[2,"مَعَارٍ"]," [with the article ",[2,"المَعَارِى"],"] signifies also (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Places that do not give growth to plants,"]," or ",[1,"herbage."]," (K.) ― -b3- And (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"Beds,"]," or ",[1,"the like;"]," syn. ",[2,"فُرُشٌ"],", (K, TA,) pl. of ",[2,"فِرَاشٌ"],". (TA.) And in this sense, (TA,) ",[2,"مَعَارِى"]," occurs for ",[2,"مَعَارٍ"],", by poetic license. (S, TA.)"]},{"h":"المَعْرَاةُ","t":[": see ",[2,"العُرْيَة"],"."]},{"h":"المُعَرَّى","t":["and ",[2,"المُعَرَّاةُ"],": see ",[2,"العُرْيَة"],", in three places. ― -b2- The former signifies also ",[1,"That"]," [camel or beast] ",[1,"which is left to pasture by itself, and upon which no burden is put."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"مُعْرَوْرًى","t":[": see ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"],", in three places."]},{"h":"مُعْرَوْرٍ","t":[": see ",[2,"عُرْىٌ"],", in two places."]}]},"mufradat":["يقال: عري من ثوبه يعرى ، فهو عار وعريان. قال تعالى: إن لك ألا تجوع فيها ولا تعرى [طه/ 118] ، وهو عرو من الذنب.","أي: عار، وأخذه عرواء أي: رعدة تعرض من العري، ومعاري الإنسان: الأعضاء التي من شأنها أن تعرى كالوجه واليد والرجل، وفلان حسن المعرى، كقولك: حسن المحسر والمجرد، والعراء: مكان لا سترة به، قال: فنبذناه بالعراء وهو سقيم [الصافات/ 145] ، والعرا مقصور: الناحية ، وعراه واعتراه: قصد عراه. قال تعالى: إلا اعتراك بعض آلهتنا بسوء [هود/ 54] . والعروة: ما يتعلق به من عراه. أي: ناحيته. قال تعالى: فقد استمسك بالعروة الوثقى [البقرة/ 256] ، وذلك على سبيل التمثيل.","والعروة أيضا: شجرة يتعلق بها الإبل، ويقال لها: عروة وعلقة. والعري والعرية: ما يعرو من الريح الباردة، والنخلة العرية: ما يعرى عن البيع وي ل، وقيل: هي التي يعريها صاحبها محتاجا، فجعل ثمرتها له ورخص أن يبتاع بتمر لموضع الحاجة، وقيل: هي النخلة للرجل وسط نخيل كثيرة لغيره، فيتأذى به صاحب الكثير ، فرخص له أن يبتاع ثمرته بتمر، والجميع العرايا. «ورخص رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم في بيع العرايا» ."]}